RUNTIME FIX AFTER PBR V4
- Target log exposed incomplete PBS HLMS shader-library registration.
- OgreNext PBS paths now come from HlmsPbs::getDefaultPaths(); do not hand-maintain them.
- Generated JSON-colour textures are ManualTexture and bound to PBS by TextureGpu pointer.
- Tangents are only submitted for materials that actually use normalMap.
- Runtime std::exceptions are caught in main so renderer failures shut down cleanly instead of std::terminate.

RUNTIME HOTFIX V6
- HLMS default paths are resolved relative to Ogre Media root, not Media/Hlms.
- HLMS initialization exceptions are caught and return a clean initialization failure.


LIGHTING FOLLOW-UP V7
- Target screenshot showed ambient fill was too weak.
- Ambient upper/lower hemisphere values increased.
- Camera flashlight added, default ON, F toggles it.
- Forward3D enabled for local PBS lights.
- Flashlight currently does not cast its own shadow map.


RUNTIME MATERIAL NOTE
PBS is linear-light. Ogre render window must use `sRGB Gamma Conversion=Yes`.
JSON solid colours are converted sRGB -> linear and sent directly to PBS background diffuse.
Diffuse texture files are loaded as sRGB; normal maps are linear.


DEBUG HUD V9
- F5 toggles top-left runtime diagnostics.
- Shows exact position group/local-cell/sub-block fractions, render-anchor local XYZ + origin block, block/chunk coords, biome weights, FPS/frame time, streaming counts, current voxel, yaw/pitch and flashlight.
- Update cadence is 200 ms; do not move biome/string formatting into the per-frame render hot path.
- Uses OGRE-Next-Overlay and requires HLMS Unlit in addition to terrain PBS.
